    <p>To multiply rational functions, we multiply the resulting rational expressions on the right side of the equation using the same techniques we used to multiply rational expressions.</p>
    <example number="7.11">
      <problem>
        <p>Find $$R(x) = f(x) \cdot g(x)$$ where $$f(x) = \frac{2x - 6}{x^{2} - 8x + 15}$$ and $$g(x) = \frac{x^{2} - 25}{2x + 10}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="Step-by-step simplification of a rational algebraic expression R(x).">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = f(x) \cdot g(x)$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = \frac{2x - 6}{x^{2} - 8x + 15} \cdot \frac{x^{2} - 25}{2x + 10}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor each numerator and denominator.</cell>
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = \frac{2\left( {x - 3} \right)}{\left( {x - 3} \right)\left( {x - 5} \right)} \cdot \frac{\left( {x - 5} \right)\left( {x + 5} \right)}{2\left( {x + 5} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply the numerators and denominators.</cell>
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = \frac{2\left( {x - 3} \right)\left( {x - 5} \right)\left( {x + 5} \right)}{2\left( {x - 3} \right)\left( {x - 5} \right)\left( {x + 5} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Remove common factors.</cell>
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = \frac{2\left( {x - 3} \right)\left( {x - 5} \right)\left( {x + 5} \right)}{2\left( {x - 3} \right)\left( {x - 5} \right)\left( {x + 5} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = 1$$</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="7.21">
      <p>Find $$R(x) = f(x) \cdot g(x)$$ where $$f(x) = \frac{3x - 21}{x^{2} - 9x + 14}$$ and $$g(x) = \frac{2x^{2} - 8}{3x + 6}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="7.22">
      <p>Find $$R(x) = f(x) \cdot g(x)$$ where $$f(x) = \frac{x^{2} - x}{3x^{2} + 27x - 30}$$ and $$g(x) = \frac{x^{2} - 100}{x^{2} - 10x}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <p>To divide rational functions, we divide the resulting rational expressions on the right side of the equation using the same techniques we used to divide rational expressions.</p>
    <example number="7.12">
      <problem>
        <p>Find $$R(x) = \frac{f(x)}{g(x)}$$ where $$f(x) = \frac{3x^{2}}{x^{2} - 4x}$$ and $$g(x) = \frac{9x^{2} - 45x}{x^{2} - 7x + 10}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="This table illustrates the step-by-step process of dividing two rational functions and simplifying the resulting expression.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = \frac{f(x)}{g(x)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Substitute in the functions $$f(x),\ g(x).$$</cell>
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = \frac{\frac{3x^{2}}{x^{2} - 4x}}{\frac{9x^{2} - 45x}{x^{2} - 7x + 10}}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite the division as the product of$$f(x)$$ and the reciprocal of $$g(x).$$</cell>
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = \frac{3x^{2}}{x^{2} - 4x} \cdot \frac{x^{2} - 7x + 10}{9x^{2} - 45x}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the numerators and denominatorsand then multiply.</cell>
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = \frac{3 \cdot x \cdot x \cdot \left( {x - 5} \right)\left( {x - 2} \right)}{x\left( {x - 4} \right) \cdot 3 \cdot 3 \cdot x \cdot \left( {x - 5} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify by dividing out common factors.</cell>
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = \frac{3 \cdot x \cdot x\left( {x - 5} \right)\left( {x - 2} \right)}{x\left( {x - 4} \right) \cdot 3 \cdot 3 \cdot x\left( {x - 5} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\qquad R(x) = \frac{x - 2}{3\left( {x - 4} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="7.23">
      <p>Find $$R(x) = \frac{f(x)}{g(x)}$$ where $$f(x) = \frac{2x^{2}}{x^{2} - 8x}$$ and $$g(x) = \frac{8x^{2} + 24x}{x^{2} + x - 6}.$$</p>
    </note>
